    "exampleHtml": "Today is the <span class=\"vp-verb\">third</span> of May. · My birthday is <span class=\"vp-prep\">on</span> the <span class=\"vp-verb\">twelfth</span> of April. · I live on the <span class=\"vp-verb\">second</span> floor.",
    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "Most ordinal numbers are the number + <strong>-th</strong>: <em>four<strong>th</strong>, six<strong>th</strong>, ten<strong>th</strong>, thirteen<strong>th</strong></em>. Three are special: <em><strong>first</strong> (1st), <strong>second</strong> (2nd), <strong>third</strong> (3rd)</em>. In figures: <em>1st, 2nd, 3rd, 4th, 21st, 22nd, 23rd, 30th</em>.",
        "tag": "The form"
      },
      {
        "html": "Watch the spelling: <em>fifth</em> (not <s>fiveth</s>), <em>eighth</em> (not <s>eightth</s>), <em>ninth</em> (not <s>nineth</s>), <em>twelfth</em> (not <s>twelveth</s>). Tens: <em>twentieth, thirtieth</em> (-y becomes -ie). After 20, only the last number changes: <em>twenty-first, twenty-second, thirty-first</em>.",
        "tag": "Spelling"
      },
      {
        "html": "In Britain, the <strong>day comes first</strong>. You write <em>3 May</em> or <em>3rd May</em>. You say <em>the third of May</em> or <em>May the third</em>. Ask: <em>What's the date today?</em> Answer: <em>It's the third of May.</em>",
        "tag": "Dates"
      },
      {
        "html": "Use <strong>on</strong> with a day or date: <em>on Monday, on 3 May, on the third of May</em>. Use <strong>in</strong> with a month or a year: <em>in May, in 2026</em>.",
        "tag": "on / in"
      },
      {
        "html": "Say a year in two parts: <em>1999 = nineteen ninety-nine</em>, <em>2026 = twenty twenty-six</em>, <em>1985 = nineteen eighty-five</em>. For 2000 to 2009: <em>two thousand and eight</em>.",
        "tag": "Years"
      },
      {
        "html": "Ordinal numbers also say the floor: <em>the second floor</em>. In Britain, the <em>ground floor</em> is at street level, and the <em>first floor</em> is one floor up. We say <em>the first time, my second job, the 21st century</em> (<em>the twenty-first century</em>).",
        "tag": "Floors and more"
      },
      {
        "html": "Typical mistakes: ✗ <em>the twelveth of May</em> → ✓ <em>the twelfth of May</em> · ✗ <em>My birthday is in 3 May.</em> → ✓ <em>My birthday is on 3 May.</em> · ✗ <em>It's the three of May.</em> → ✓ <em>It's the third of May.</em>",
        "tag": "Typical mistakes"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "In American English the month comes first: <em>May 3</em>, said <em>May third</em>. So <em>03/05/2026</em> is 3 May in the UK but 5 March in the US. For <em>on, in</em> and <em>at</em> with times, see <a href=\"/prepositions-of-time\">Prepositions of time</a>. For cardinal numbers (one, two, three), see <a href=\"/numbers\">Numbers</a>.",
